# Signals from data

Before writing a prompt that asks a model to guess something about the
person (activity, company, sleep, mood, place), check whether their own data
already shows it. Follow `docs/BIM_SIGNALS_PLAYBOOK.md`: find ground truth they
made, measure a cheap signal against a baseline on the real files, ship the
winner as a counted fact in `Evidence.facts` (constants learned at run time,
`null` when there are too few cases), and add the result, good or bad, to the
playbook's table. Texts older than a few weeks are not evidence of the present.
